  "speaker": "grandma",
  "voiceId": "9c633ca4a45a4e9ba74cb36cfa21fb00",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free",
  "text": "Today Pip brought me Mara’s explanation. Her work hours had changed. While I was waiting here, she was waiting for the last passengers to come ashore. Then I asked Sol what had kept him away. He thought no one would want to hear about the ordinary things he made and fixed.\n\nMy small boat can carry the seed, but it cannot carry Pip. Load the seed at the yellow launch. Steer around the rock to my blue landing. I will come to collect the seed and bring it to our planting spot. You may also carry the seed across the secured bridge.\n\nMara brought stories about people she met at the dock. Sometimes she began laughing before she reached the funny part. Sol told us about things he had made. He would hold his hands apart to show the size of something, and we would have to move our cups.\n\n“The garden is quiet these days. Mara and Sol hardly visit anymore. I think they don’t enjoy coming now. Yesterday I thought I heard someone on the path, but it was only the leaves. I miss their stories. I’m glad you and I have a seed to plant.”\n\nWalk onto the secured first section. Bring the second section into place and connect the short ends. Seat the two far corner posts. Extend each rope from its center post to the matching far corner post, then wrap, tighten and tie it.\n\n“Hold on,” I said, mostly to the cloth. It flapped across the table toward a jug of water. Sol caught it before it knocked the jug over. For a moment we stood with our arms stretched out, looking at each other over the table.\n\nSecure a rope along each side of the first section, from a near corner post to a center post. Wrap each rope around its posts, pull it taut and tie a knot. Both sides must be secure before you put your weight on this section.",
  "textSha256": "5c818394c1c07e8398537c766cb5140e59b9da04e6123877d30b09ed4d310550",
